# Counter-example: two distinct graphemes of the GMN script related by
# gmeow:gmnConfusableWith — U+00B5 MICRO SIGN and U+03BC GREEK SMALL LETTER MU, the
# canonical UTS #39 skeleton pair for μ admitted into one inventory (fires
# lang:GmnConfusableGlyph via the sh:sparql of lang:GmnConfusableGlyphShape). Both
# graphemes are otherwise well-formed: grounded in the repertoire, canonical codepoints,
# DISTINCT codepoint values (U+00B5 vs U+03BC, so lang:GmnGlyphCollisionShape stays quiet),
# and each carries its measured gmeow:gmnGlyphTokenCost feed (so
# lang:GmnScriptGlyphCoverageShape's total glyph-cost coverage stays satisfied and
# lang:GmnUncostedScriptGlyph stays quiet) — exactly the one confusable-pair finding fires.

@prefix lang:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/lang/> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/lang/> .

gmeow:gmnScript lang:hasGrapheme ex:gMicroSign , ex:gGreekMu .

ex:gMicroSign a lang:Grapheme ;
    lang:inScript gmeow:gmnScript ;
    gmeow:gmnCodepoints "U+00B5" ;
    gmeow:gmnGlyphTokenCost ex:qCostOne ;
    gmeow:gmnConfusableWith ex:gGreekMu .

ex:gGreekMu a lang:Grapheme ;
    lang:inScript gmeow:gmnScript ;
    gmeow:gmnCodepoints "U+03BC" ;
    gmeow:gmnGlyphTokenCost ex:qCostOne .

ex:qCostOne a math:Quantity ;
    math:hasDimension math:dimensionless ;
    math:quantityValue 1 .
